\sectionbox{1. Data Design Overview}
MorningBrief.AI utilizes \textbf{Supabase (PostgreSQL)} for persistent storage. Our data architecture is designed to handle two distinct types of information:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Persistent Entities:} Core user data, preferences, and user-generated content (Todos, Diaries) that remain in the database.
    \item \textbf{Runtime Entities (API Cache):} Dynamic data fetched from external providers (OpenWeather, Google Calendar, News API). These are stored in a centralized \texttt{ApiCache} table to minimize API costs and improve performance.
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{Key Attributes Description}
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{UserSettings.vis (JSONB):} A flexible mapping of widget IDs to boolean values, allowing users to toggle specific dashboard components.
    \item \textbf{Todo.is\_fixed (Boolean):} Differentiates between one-time tasks and recurring daily routines that survive the nightly cleanup process.
    \item \textbf{ApiCache.cache\_key (String):} A unique identifier generated based on request parameters (e.g., coordinates or search terms) to manage TTL (Time-To-Live).
    \item \textbf{BriefingWidget (Aggregation):} This is a virtual entity representing the data context sent to the \textbf{Groq LLM} to generate the personalized "Morning Briefing" text.
\end{itemize}

