\sectionbox{3. Data Associations}
\textbf{Entity Relationships:}
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{User $\to$ UserSettings / WidgetLayouts (1:1):} Each user profile is strictly mapped to one set of configuration and layout preferences.
    \item \textbf{User $\to$ Todo / Diary / SmartKeyword (1:N):} A user can manage multiple tasks, history logs, and custom monitoring keywords.
    \item \textbf{ApiCache $\to$ Dynamic Entities (1:1/1:N):} The cache serves as a proxy for external entities. For example, one \texttt{ApiCache} entry might store a single \texttt{Weather} object or a list of \texttt{Stock} objects.
\end{itemize}

\sectionbox{4. Front-end Web View Plan}
The UI is implemented using \textbf{React.js} and \textbf{Tailwind CSS} for a responsive, modular dashboard. 
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Modular Widgets:} Each data entity in the UML corresponds to a dedicated UI component.
    \item \textbf{State Management:} Runtime data is managed via React hooks, synchronized with the Supabase \texttt{ApiCache} to ensure seamless updates without redundant network requests.
\end{itemize}

